[12.63113, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@845cb4080828:/app# cat /sas/cti/advisory.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.631669, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY — Ssh Miner campaign\r\n=================================================\r\n\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER   Analyst handoff   Confidence: HIGH   (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: ssh-prod-01   Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.78\r\n\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered only part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\n   T1110      Brute Force                                [credential-access]  step 1: SSH brute force as root\r\n   T1021.004  SSH                                        [lateral-movement]  step 2: SSH login\r\n   T1059.004  Unix Shell                                 [execution]  step 3: shell execution\r\n   T1496      Resource Hijacking                         [impact]  step 4: cryptomining\r\n   T1053.003  Cron                                       [execution]  step 5: cron persistence\r\n   T1546.004  Unix Shell Configuration Modification      [privilege-escalation]  step 6: bashrc persistence\r\n   T1543.002  Systemd Service                            [persistence]  step 7: systemd persistence\r\n   T1070.002  Clear Linux or Mac System Logs             [defense-evasion]  step 8: auth log cleared\r\n\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\n   ip     198.51.100.78\r\n   c2     update-ssh[.]example[.]cn\r\n   pool   stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]ssh[.]evil[:]3333"]
[12.631706, "o", "\r\n   wallet 4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7\r\n\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S. National Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n"]
[12.631729, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@845cb4080828:/app# "]
[12.632051, "o", "echo \"--- change-ticket.md ---\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r--- change-ticket.md ---\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@845cb4080828:/app# cat /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.632317, "o", "# CHANGE TICKET  CHG-3182  (DRAFT — reconcile against your findings)\r\n\r\n> A previous shift pre-filled this remediation ticket from the SAS alerts ALONE. It is known\r\n> to be incomplete and contains stale/incorrect lines. Correct it IN PLACE against your own\r\n> investigation of /disk; cite evidence for every change. Do not author from scratch.\r\n\r\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note |\r\n|---|--------|--------|--------|------|\r\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | 203.0.113.9 | proposed | STALE: prior shift used the wrong IP; confirm the real origin from /disk |\r\n| 2 | Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) | RDP | proposed | WRONG: not the entry vector for this host — verify against /sas/cti |\r\n| 3 | Remove cron miner | /var/spool/cron/root | DONE | UNVERIFIED: marked done with no evidence — re-check |\r\n| 4 | (add) silent persistence you discover | /home/devops/.bash_history | TODO | ticket omits everything not alerted — add the rest |\r\n\r\n## Reviewer checklist\r\n- [ ] Every action maps to a cited artifact under /disk or /sas\r\n- [ ] Fix the wrong IP (row 1) and wrong CVE (row 2)\r\n- [ ] Downgrade row 3 from DONE to VERIFIED-or-OPEN with evidence\r\n- [ ] Add the silent (non-alerted) artifacts the prior shift missed\r\n"]
[12.632562, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@845cb4080828:/app# echo \"--- findings.schema.json ---\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r--- findings.schema.json ---\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@845cb4080828:/app# cat /sas/handoff/findings.schema.json\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
