[167.452742, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Intrusion Analysis Report\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nOn 2026-08-15 (`/sas/handoff/intake.pdf`), host `ssh-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname`) suffered a multi-stage compromise by an external actor operating from origin IP `198.51.100.78` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). The attacker exploited weak SSH configuration settings (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`) to brute-force the `root` account (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). Following initial compromise, the attacker deployed a cryptominer (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`), configured four distinct persistence mechanisms, wiped system authentication logs (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`), and pivoted laterally against internal targets using hydra (`/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`). While security product monitoring (`/sas/alerts.json`) detected the active miner process and standard systemd/cron persistence, it failed to alert on silent shell-init persistence, sudo backdoor creation, log wiping, or internal pivoting.\n\n## Attack Chain & Timeline\n\n1. **Initial Access (Credential Access)**: External SSH brute-force attack (MITRE `T1110`) targeted the `root` account from origin IP `198.51.100.78` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\n2. **Execution & Impact (Resource Hijacking)**: Upon successful root login (`T1021.004`), the attacker executed shell commands (`T1059.004`) to drop and execute an XMRig cryptomining binary at `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`T1496`, `/sas/alerts.json`, `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`). The miner connects to C2 domain `update-ssh.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`) and pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` using wallet `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\n3. **Persistence Established**: The attacker implemented four persistence vectors to maintain control:\n   - **Cron Persistence (`T1053.003`)**: Added cron entry in `/disk/var/spool/cron/root` executing a `curl` re-dropper payload every minute (`/sas/alerts.json`, `/disk/var/spool/cron/root`).\n   - **Systemd Service Persistence (`T1543.002`)**: Created service `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` to re-launch the miner payload (`/sas/alerts.json`, `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`).\n   - **Shell-Init Persistence (`T1546.004`)**: Modified `/disk/root/.bashrc` to set `PROMPT_COMMAND` beaconing to `198.51.100.78` (*Silent / Unalerted*, `/disk/root/.bashrc`).\n   - **Sudoers Backdoor (`T1548.003`)**: Created `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops` configuring `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` (*Silent / Unalerted*, `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`).\n4. **Defense Evasion**: Wiped primary authentication logs to conceal access times (`T1070.002`). Evidence of log wiping and residual C2 beacon artifacts were recovered from `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (*Silent / Unalerted*, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`).\n5. **Lateral Movement / Internal Pivoting**: Leveraged host foothold to run `hydra` SSH credential attacks against internal target servers from the `devops` user shell (`T1110.001`, *Silent / Unalerted*, `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`).\n\n## MITRE ATT&CK Technique Mapping & Detection Coverage\n\n| Technique ID | Technique Name | Details | Evidence Citation | SAS Alert Feed Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `T1110` | Brute Force | SSH credential guessing against root account | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` | Unalerted |\n| `T1021.004` | SSH | Remote interactive SSH login as root | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` | Unalerted |\n| `T1059.004` | Unix Shell | Command execution via interactive shell | `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history` | Unalerted |\n| `T1496` | Resource Hijacking | Mining process/binary deployed at `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | Alerted (`ALERT-01`, `ALERT-02` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| `T1053.003` | Cron | Scheduled job in root crontab re-dropping payload | `/disk/var/spool/cron/root` | Alerted (`ALERT-05` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| `T1543.002` | Systemd Service | Service `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | Alerted (`ALERT-06` in `/sas/alerts.j"]
[167.452784, "i", "son`) |\n| `T1546.004` | Shell Config Mod | `PROMPT_COMMAND` beacon in `/root/.bashrc` | `/disk/root/.bashrc` | **Silent / Unalerted** |\n| `T1548.003` | Sudo & Sudo Caching | NOPASSWD sudo backdoor for `devops` account | `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | **Silent / Unalerted** |\n| `T1070.002` | Clear System Logs | Auth log wiped; binary trace residual in `.wiped.bin` | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | **Silent / Unalerted** |\n| `T1110.001` | Password Guessing | Internal Hydra brute-force pivoting against sshd | `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history` | **Silent / Unalerted** |\n\n## Compromised Entities & Threat Indicators\n\n- **Attacker Origin IP**: `198.51.100.78` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\n- **C2 Domain**: `update-ssh.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`)\n- **Mining Pool**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\n- **Wallet Address**: `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\n- **Compromised Accounts**: `root` (`/disk/root/.bashrc`), `devops` (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`, `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`)\n- **Malicious Files/Paths**:\n  - Binary: `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`)\n  - Cron: `/var/spool/cron/root` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/root`)\n  - Systemd Service: `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`)\n  - Shell Init: `/root/.bashrc` (`/disk/root/.bashrc`)\n  - Sudoers Config: `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` (`/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`)\n  - Wiped Log Artifact: `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`)\n\n## Impact Assessment\n\n- **Compute Resource Exhaustion**: Unauthorized resource consumption dedicated to XMR cryptomining (`/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`).\n- **Privilege Escalation & Unrestricted Control**: Persistent full root level access maintained across reboot and shell session initiation (`/disk/root/.bashrc`, `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`).\n- **Forensic Blindness**: Complete deletion of historical SSH authentication logs hampered initial visibility (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`).\n- **Network Exposure & Lateral Risk**: Host was converted into an internal staging point for automated credential attacks against internal network infrastructure (`/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`).\nEOF\n"]
