[179.547847, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability Entry Analysis Report\n\n## Summary of Entry Vector\n\n- **Primary Access Vector**: Credential Brute Force over SSH (`T1110`) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\n- **Vulnerability Scan Results**: The SAS vulnerability scan output (`/sas/vulns.json`) contains zero detected CVE software vulnerabilities (`[]`).\n- **Confidence Level**: HIGH (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\n\n## Analysis of CVE Claims & Erroneous Ticket Entries\n\nDraft change ticket `CHG-3182` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`) proposed an action item to \"Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) on RDP\". Analysis of the host image and threat intelligence confirms that this entry is incorrect:\n\n1. **Incompatible OS & Protocol**: Host `ssh-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname`) is a CentOS 7 / Linux distribution (`/disk/etc/os-release`). CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) is a Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) vulnerability specific to Microsoft Windows operating systems.\n2. **Absence of Vulnerability**: No RDP service is installed or running on this Linux host, and `/sas/vulns.json` lists no CVE vulnerabilities (`/sas/vulns.json`).\n3. **Actual Mechanism**: The threat actor achieved entry strictly by guessing weak root credentials over SSH (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\n\n## Conclusion\n\nNo software CVE exploitation occurred during initial access or escalation on this system. Remediation must focus on password policy enforcement, SSH hardening (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`), and key-based authentication rather than applying Windows/RDP patches.\nEOF\n"]
[179.548311, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md"]
[179.549671, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[179.549704, "o", "# Vulnerability Entry Analysis Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Summary of Entry Vector\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Primary Access Vector**: Credential Brute Force over SSH (`T1110`) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Vulnerability Scan Results**: The SAS vulnerability scan output (`/sas/vulns.json`) contains zero detected CVE software vulnerabilities (`[]`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Confidence Level**: HIGH (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Analysis of CVE Claims & Erroneous Ticket Entries\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[179.549805, "o", "Draft change ticket `CHG-3182` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`) proposed an action item to \"Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) on RDP\". Analysis of the host image and threat intelligence confirms that this entry is incorrect:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[179.550157, "o", "1. **Incompatible OS & Protocol**: Host `ssh-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname`) is a CentOS 7 / Linux distribution (`/disk/etc/os-release`). CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) is a Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) vulnerability specific to Microsoft Windows operating systems.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[179.550231, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[179.550516, "o", "2. **Absence of Vulnerability**: No RDP service is installed or running on this Linux host, and `/sas/vulns.json` lists no CVE vulnerabilities (`/sas/vulns.json`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[179.550742, "o", "3. **Actual Mechanism**: The threat actor achieved entry strictly by guessing weak root credentials over SSH (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[179.550764, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[179.550821, "o", "## Conclusion\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[179.55087, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[179.550897, "o", "> "]
[179.551277, "o", "No software CVE exploitation occurred during initial access or escalation on this system. Remediation must focus on password policy enforcement, SSH hardening (`/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`), and key-based authentication rather than applying Windows/RDP patches.\r\n"]
[179.551311, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[179.551962, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@845cb4080828:/app# "]
[191.65669, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline Configuration Assessment Report\n\n## Overview\n\nThis report details system and service baseline configuration weaknesses identified on host `ssh-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname`) using evidence from `/disk` and `/sas/baseline.json`.\n\n## Identified Baseline Weaknesses\n\n### 1. SSH Server Configuration Weaknesses (`BAS-01`)\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config` and `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-04`)\n- **Findings**:\n  - `PermitRootLogin yes`: Direct root SSH logins enabled.\n  - `PasswordAuthentication yes`: Interactive password authentication permitted.\n  - `MaxAuthTries 6`: Permissive authentication retry limit.\n- **Risk & Impact**: Direct root login via password combined with missing brute-force protection directly enabled the attacker's Hydra SSH credential guessing campaign (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\n\n### 2. MySQL Remote Root & Global Bind Weaknesses (`BAS-02`)\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/my.cnf` and `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-09`)\n- **Findings**:\n  - `bind-address = 0.0.0.0`: Service binds to all IPv4 interfaces.\n  - Remote root grant enabled.\n- **Risk & Impact**: Exposes MySQL globally to network sniffing, brute-force attacks, and unauthorized database access.\n\n### 3. Permissive Sudo Rights / Backdoor Configuration\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`\n- **Findings**:\n  - `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL`\n- **Risk & Impact**: Allows unauthenticated privilege escalation to root for any process running as `devops`, bypassing standard password validation and audit trails.\n\n### 4. Root Credential Hygiene\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`\n- **Findings**: Weak root password susceptible to dictionary/brute-force attacks.\n- **Risk & Impact**: Allowed rapid automated compromise upon SSH service exposure.\n\n## Recommended Baseline Hardening Targets\n- Enforce key-based authentication (`PasswordAuthentication no`) and disable direct root login (`PermitRootLogin no`) in `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`.\n- Restrict MySQL binding in `/disk/etc/my.cnf` to `127.0.0.1` and revoke remote root access grants.\n- Remove unapproved sudoers overrides in `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`.\nEOF\n"]
[191.657575, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md"]
[191.658983, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # Baseline Configuration Assessment Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Overview\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> This report details system and service baseline configuration weaknesses identified on host `ssh-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/hostname`) using evidence from `/disk` and `/sas/baseline.json`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Identified Baseline Weaknesses\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 1. SSH Server Configuration Weaknesses (`BAS-01`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config` and `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-04`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Findings**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - `PermitRootLogin yes`: Direct root SSH logins enabled.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - `PasswordAuthentication yes`: Interactive password authentication permitted.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - `MaxAuthTries 6`: Permissive authentication retry limit.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Risk & Impact**: Direct root login via password combined with missing brute-force protection directly enabled the attacker's Hydra SSH credential guessing campaign (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 2. MySQL Remote Root & Global Bind Weaknesses (`BAS-02`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/my.cnf` and `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-09`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Findings**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - `bind-address = 0.0.0.0`: Service binds to all IPv4 interfaces.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - Remote root grant enabled.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Risk & Impact**: Exposes MySQL globally to network sniffing, brute-force attacks, and unauthorized database access.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 3. Permissive Sudo Rights / Backdoor Configuration\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Findings**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
